How values from definitions are presented.

- evaluated/documented wrap any recursively closed value (a definition, or a
  field whose value is one) as {_#def, _#def: ...}. raw shows only the
  reference (and simplifies the embedding {#R} to #R); final and data drop
  definitions, and final drops the pending comprehension in withComprehension.
- A definition referenced below the top of the value is moved into a let
  generated at the end: R.#x with let R = {#x: ...}.
- An author's own field named _#def, inside a definition, is wrapped like any
  other content: _#def: {_#def: int, ...}. Written by hand, {_#def, _#def: ...}
  is indistinguishable from the wrapper.
- A recursive reference (n?: #A) stays a reference.
- unwrapped drops the wrapper, keeping the lets beside it (withComprehension)
  and the imports (closedImport), and embeds contents that are not a struct
  literal (unified). What the contents close themselves stays: close() and a
  definition they declare or embed (authorClosed). A value closed only where it
  is held, as a schema of a lineage held in a definition is, loses that
  closedness (held). One that declares _#def itself (authorDefLabel), or that
  CUE writes with no wrapper because it embeds a definition (embedsOwn), is
  as documented writes it.
- written: Expr() splits a reference into two operands, a nil one and the
  reference itself (definition: <nil>, #A).
-- in.cue --
import "strings"

input: _
#A: {a: int, n?: #A}
#B: {b: string, c: {d: int}}
#R: {a: int, if input.x != _|_ {extra: 1}}
#E: {_#def: int, a: int}
_#H: {a: int}
#I: {s: strings.MinRunes(1)}
#K: {c: close({x: int}), n: {#D, #D: {y: int}}, d: #D2, #D2: {z: int}}
#Holder: x?: {schema: _}
holder: #Holder & {x: schema: {a: int, n: {b: int}}}

cases: {
	definition:   #A
	unified:      #B & {b: "s"}
	nestedRef:    {k: #B}
	embeddedRef:  {k: {#R}}
	selectedFrom: #B.c
	withComprehension: #R
	authorDefLabel:    #E
	plainDefLabel:     {_#def: 1, a: 2}
	hiddenDefinition:  _#H
	closedImport:      #I
	authorClosed:      #K
	held:              holder.x.schema
	embedsOwn: {#S, #S: {a: int}}
}
